### Logowanie – zapisuje token w zmiennej globalnej {{token}}
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### Logowanie błędnym hasłem – 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "zle-haslo"
}

### Zmiana hasła z błędnym bieżącym hasłem – 403
PUT {{host}}/api/auth/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "zle-haslo",
  "newPassword": "NoweHaslo-123456"
}

### Zmiana hasła bez tokenu – 401
PUT {{host}}/api/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "NoweHaslo-123456"
}

### Zmiana hasła – 204 (pamiętaj o przywróceniu poprzedniego hasła)
PUT {{host}}/api/auth/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "NoweHaslo-123456"
}

### Wylogowanie – 204; potem token daje 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Użycie tokenu po wylogowaniu – 401
GET {{host}}/api/sensors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
